course: dictionary
lesson: 5569
title: Lessen: getting smaller
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lessen is a verb, an action word. It means to make something smaller, weaker or less, or to become smaller or less. «A helmet lessens the risk of a head injury» tells you the helmet makes the risk smaller. It does not get rid of the risk completely.
explain: Look for the clue in the sentence. In «Talking to a friend lessened her worry», the worry is what gets smaller, so lessened must mean made less. Try swapping in «made smaller» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Lessen can also describe something becoming weaker or less, as in «the wind lessened». Lessen is different from less, which is a word for a smaller amount, not an action.
fact: Lessen is a verb: lessen, lessens, lessened, lessening.
fact: «Lessen» means to make something smaller, weaker or less, or to become smaller or less.
fact: You can lessen pain, noise, danger, worry or risk.
fact: «The wind lessened» means the wind became weaker.
fact: In «they're called lessons, because they lessen from day to day», lessen means get smaller.
exercise: «A helmet lessens the risk of a head injury.» What does lessens mean here? | Stops moving | Makes bigger | Breaks into pieces | *Makes smaller
exercise: «Talking to a friend lessened her worry.» Her worry became | Bigger | *Smaller | Louder | Shinier
exercise: «Lessons lasted ten hours the first day, nine the next.» Lessons lessen from day to day. What does this mean? | They change colour each day | They stay the same length each day | They get longer each day | *They get shorter each day
test: «Insulation lessens heat loss.» Which word is the past tense of lessen? | lessons | lessen | lessening | *lessened
test: Which phrase means to make the pain smaller? | lessening the sky | lessen the colour | lessons the pain | *lessen the pain
exam: Which sentence uses lessen to mean become smaller? | Please lessen the sound of the rain | Lessen is a verb | *The wind lessened all afternoon | We had lessons today
